  "slug": "reveals-potassium-0e35",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend low-input LC-MS, single-cell, and native MS methods to protein complexes and viral glycoproteins.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the development and benchmarking of mass spectrometry and single-molecule workflows that improve sensitivity, analysis, and molecular resolution. Trap column benchmarking addresses low-input LC-MS proteomics, comparing a NanoShield trap column family against PepMap and direct injection across bed length, flush direction, and pore characteristics. Software contributions include OSMSS, a no-code R Shiny application for differential abundance, phosphosite, and enrichment analysis, and SCP-Viz, a visual toolkit tested on dried, room-temperature-stored single cancer cell digests. On the molecular side, super-resolved mass photometry links successive binding events to individual complexes to reveal dissociation pathways, while DIA-ECCR native mass spectrometry resolves intact SARS-CoV-2 spike glycoform distributions and heparan sulfate binding across variants. Across these items, the advance is pairing resolution at the level of single molecules and intact assemblies with analysis tools usable by non-specialists.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
